Stop this package's indexers from answering for every catalog. `login` and `SearchableText` were declared for the Profile alone, which registers an indexer against any catalog that asks — and a Profile is ordinary content, catalogued in `portal_catalog` as well. So a Profile's entry in site search was its full name, login and email, and its biography was not searchable at all. Both are now bound to the identity catalog, where they are unchanged, and site search gets an answer of its own: the title, the userid and the biography. Neither the login nor the address, which have no business in a site's search box. @ericof
